832648277283,"seed":895194184519585109,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we start by analyzing the functional equation given: \\( f(x) = f(x+1) + f(x-1) \\). We can rewrite this equation as:\n\\[ f(x+1) = f(x) - f(x-1). \\]\n\nThis suggests that the function might exhibit periodic behavior. Let's explore the values of the function for a few terms to identify a pattern.\n\nFirst, we calculate \\( f(x+2) \\):\n\\[ f(x+2) = f(x+1+1) = f(x+1) - f(x) = (f(x) - f(x-1)) - f(x) = -f(x-1). \\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( f(x+3) \\):\n\\[ f(x+3) = f(x+2+1) = f(x+2) - f(x+1) = -f(x-1) - (f(x) - f(x-1)) = -f(x). \\]\n\nThen, we calculate \\( f(x+4) \\):\n\\[ f(x+4) = f(x+3+1) = f(x+3) - f(x+2) = -f(x) - (-f(x-1)) = -f(x) + f(x-1). \\]\n\nFinally, we calculate \\( f(x+5) \\):\n\\[ f(x+5) = f(x+4+1) = f(x+4) - f(x+3) = (-f(x) + f(x-1)) - (-f(x)) = f(x-1). \\]\n\nFrom the above calculations, we observe that:\n\\[ f(x+5) = f(x-1). \\]\n\nThis implies that:\n\\[ f(x+6) = f(x). \\]\n\nThus, the function \\( f(x) \\) is periodic with a period of 6. To find \\( f(20152015) \\), we need to determine the remainder when 20152015 is divided by 6:\n\\[ 20152015 \\div 6 = 3358669 \\text{ remainder } 1. \\]\n\nTherefore,\n\\[ 20152015 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6}. \\]\n\nThis means:\n\\[ f(20152015) = f(1). \\]\n\nTo find \\( f(1) \\), we use the given values \\( f(15) = 20 \\) and \\( f(20) = 15 \\). Since the function is periodic with period 6:\n\\[ f(15) = f(15 \\mod 6) = f(3) = 20, \\]\n\\[ f(20) = f(20 \\mod 6) = f(2) = 15. \\]\n\nWe also know:\n\\[ f(3) = f(2+1) = f(2) - f(1) = 15 - f(1) = 20. \\]\n\nSolving for \\( f(1) \\):\n\\[ 15 - f(1) = 20, \\]\n\\[ -f(1) = 5, \\]\n\\[ f(1) = -5. \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( f(20152015) \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{-5}. \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-5}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
